# Mi Pad 2 test no-idle mode

This is deliberately opt-in. Enable it for kernel/camera/suspend testing:

```sh
sudo mp2-test-no-idle enable
```

It inhibits idle blanking, suspend, and lid-triggered sleep, and changes only
the GNOME power settings needed for the test. Previous GNOME values are saved
and restored by:

```sh
sudo mp2-test-no-idle disable
```

It does not modify Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, display scaling, kernel selection, or
Secure Boot settings.
